---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { scenes } from '../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import NewsletterForm from '../components/NewsletterForm.astro';
const crumbs = [{ label: 'Newsletter', href: '/newsletter/' }];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Sky This Month: Mo's free monthly letter"
  description="A free monthly note from Mo Lumen: current sky, questions worth following, and the ideas she has been thinking about across astrology, cycles, nature, and lived experience."
  path="/newsletter/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">A monthly note from Mo</p>
      <h1>The Sky This Month</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Once a month I send a letter about what has caught my attention: something moving in the
        sky, a pattern I keep noticing, a question worth carrying for a while, or a connection I
        have been thinking about. Current Sky is part of it, but the letter is broader than a
        forecast. It is correspondence.
      </p>
      </div>
      <img
        class="hero__img"
        src={scenes.newsletterLetters.src}
        srcset={scenes.newsletterLetters.srcset}
        sizes="100vw"
        alt={scenes.newsletterLetters.alt}
        width={scenes.newsletterLetters.width}
        height={scenes.newsletterLetters.height}
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid grid--2" style="align-items: start;">
      <div class="flow">
        <h2 id="nl-signup">Join the list</h2>
        <NewsletterForm source="newsletter-page" labelledby="nl-signup" />
        <p class="card__meta">
          Your email is used for this newsletter only, never sold, never shared. Marketing
          consent is always separate from booking. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card flow">
        <p class="eyebrow">If you want to read first</p>
        <h2 style="font-size: var(--text-xl); margin: 0;">See what the letter grows out of</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="/current-sky/">Current Sky</a> follows the cycles overhead as they happen.
          <a href="/blog/">The blog</a> is where longer ideas have room to develop, and
          <a href="/explore/">Explore Astrology</a> teaches the language and structure underneath
          both. None requires an email address.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>What tends to appear in the letter</h2>
      <p>
        The mix changes because attention changes. You may find a Current Sky observation, a
        question that stayed with me after studying a chart, something from biology or the natural
        world that sharpened the way I was thinking about cycles, or a note about a new article,
        guide, or class when there is actually something ready to share.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am not trying to turn every month into instructions. I would rather give you something
        worth noticing and leave room for you to decide what, if anything, it means in your own
        life.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
